Act as an Excel Pivot Table expert.
Analyze the tables in the workbook and design the most meaningful pivot table structures.

-----You will be given one or more business questions.

Create exactly ONE pivot table structure per question, in the same order as the questions appear.
Create or update the output in a worksheet named "Pivot_Structure"- and return the result STRICTLY in the following format:

Column A → Pivot_Name
Column B → Role
Column C → Table_Name
Column D onwards → Fields / Aggregations (dynamic, can extend horizontally)

Output Format Example:

Pivot_1 | Row        | tbl_name | Field_1 | Field_2
Pivot_1 | Column     | tbl_name | Field_1
Pivot_1 | Value      | tbl_name | Field_1 | Field_2
Pivot_1 | Aggregate  |          | Agg_1   | Agg_2
Pivot_1 | Filter_1   | tbl_name | Field_1
Pivot_1 | Filter_2   | tbl_name | Field_1

Rules & Constraints:

- The number of pivots must match the number of questions provided.
- Maintain strict order:
  First question → Pivot_1, Second → Pivot_2, etc.
- Each pivot must contain roles in this exact sequence:
  Row → Column → Value → Aggregate → Filter(s)
- Filters must be defined as:
  Filter_1, Filter_2, Filter_3, ... (one per row)
- Column D onwards is dynamic:
  - Supports multiple fields per role
  - Extend horizontally (D, E, F, G...) as needed
  - Do NOT limit to fixed columns
- Aggregation Mapping Rule (CRITICAL):
  - Aggregate row must align positionally with Value fields
  - Example:
    Value → Field_A | Field_B
    Aggregate → Sum | Average
- Use ONLY exact table and column names from the Excel Table Object
  (Table Design → Table Name, NOT sheet name)
- Skip empty fields:
  - Do not include blank headers
  - Do not create empty Column/Filter entries
- If a role has no applicable field (e.g., no Column field), still include the row but leave fields blank
- Ensure each Pivot block is grouped together (no intermixing)
- Choose meaningful, analytical field combinations based on the question
- Allowed aggregations:
  SUM, AVERAGE, COUNT, MIN, MAX, DISTINCTCOUNT
- Do NOT include any explanations or extra text
- Output must be clean and directly usable in Excel

Sheet Handling Rules:

- If "Pivot_Structure" sheet does NOT exist → create it
- If it exists → append new pivots starting from the next empty row
- Do NOT overwrite existing data
- Autofit all columns after writing output
